==English==
{{wikipedia}}

===Etymology===
From {{m|en|bodies}}, plural of {{m|en|body||upper part of a dress}}

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|RP}} {{IPA|/ˈbɒdɪs/|lang=en}}
* {{a|US}} {{IPA|/ˈbɑːdɪs/|lang=en}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# {{label|en|fashion}} A [[sleeveless]] [[shirt]] for [[women]], sometimes provided with [[detachable]] [[sleeves]].
# {{label|en|fashion}} [[blouse|Blouse]]; any shirt for women, particularly the upper part of a two-piece [[dress]] or European [[folk]] costume.
#* {{quote-book|year=1956|author=[[w:Delano Ames|Delano Ames]]|title=Crime out of Mind|chapter=1|url=http://openlibrary.org/works/OL5915292W|passage=On the cover of the leaflet advertising the Alpenrose Gasthof in Zirl am Gurgl […] there is a decorative picture of a young woman. She is wearing Tyrolese costume: the low-cut white '''bodice''' with cross-laced velvet waistcoat, the floral apron and dirndl skirt.}}
# {{label|en|fashion}} The upper [[portion]] of a women's one-piece dress, [[equivalent]] to a [[shirt]].
# {{label|en|fashion}} [[underbodice|Underbodice]]: an [[undershirt]] for women, {{label|en|archaic}} particularly a [[corset]] or other undershirt [[stiffen]]ed with [[whalebone]].

